@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+No P1 findings. The billing path is sound, and the existing candidate predicate does not expose private, link-shared, archived, or unopenable articles. I found six changes needed before building.
+
+1. **P2 — This is a new discovery surface, even though it exposes only public articles.**  
+   Evidence: the plan says the result reveals nothing beyond `/read/public` and the public page ([plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/plans/261009j-a-public-copy-offered-at-import.md:43)), but `/read/public` is capped at 200 articles ([public-library.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/store/public-library.ts:88)), while `citedCandidates` is deliberately unbounded ([pg-cited-in-spideryarn.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/store/pg-cited-in-spideryarn.ts:48)). The security map explicitly distinguishes knowing a public article’s unguessable slug from being able to discover it through a listing ([security-map.md](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/project/security-map.md:193)). This endpoint lets an authenticated caller who knows or guesses a source URL discover an older public article’s slug and title; paper-source equivalence can also find it through a different public URL.  
+   The predicate itself is safe: it requires public, unarchived, tree plus blocks ([pg-cited-in-spideryarn.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/store/pg-cited-in-spideryarn.ts:92)), strips stranger-only metadata ([pg-cited-in-spideryarn.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/store/pg-cited-in-spideryarn.ts:103)), and link-shared articles remain private ([security-map.md](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/project/security-map.md:304)).  
+   **Fix:** explicitly authorize and document this as a new authenticated source-URL lookup in the plan and security map, rather than claiming no new discoverability. Add canaries for link-shared/private, archived, unopenable, title override, `requested_url`/`asked_url`, and query- or credential-bearing `final_url`. If no new discoverability is acceptable, restrict candidates to the same rows visible in the capped public listing.
+
+2. **P2 — The module-level `PrivateCopy` one-shot is not a sound navigation intent.**  
+   Evidence: the proposed mark is set before navigation and deliberately disappears in a new tab ([plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/plans/261009j-a-public-copy-offered-at-import.md:101)). `Link` invokes its supplied `onClick` before deciding whether the click is a Command/Ctrl/Shift click or targets another tab ([Link.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/web/Link.tsx:37)). Therefore a Command-click can set the mark in the original tab, open an unmarked new tab, and leave the stale mark to make a later ordinary paste skip the offer and attempt a paid import. A module-level mark can likewise survive an interrupted navigation or account change.  
+   **Fix:** encode the intent in a durable distinct route, such as `/add-own/<encoded-address>`, parsed into `{ kind: "add", url, ownCopy: true }`. Include the intent in `addAddress` so account-change and visit guards distinguish it. This works for plain clicks, new tabs, reloads, and copied links without mutable global state. Test modified clicks, cold loads, StrictMode, and reader changes.
+
+3. **P2 — A public-copy answer must not enter `Completion` or any slug-owning Add-page machinery.**  
+   Evidence: `Completion` means “the article this add became” ([AddPage.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/web/AddPage.tsx:134)). Its slug is immediately observed by High-powered AI ([AddPage.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/web/AddPage.tsx:1050)), sharing ([AddPage.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/web/AddPage.tsx:1094)), and the purpose session ([AddPage.tsx](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/web/AddPage.tsx:1130)). The public article belongs to somebody else; treating its slug like the repeat article could issue owner-only PUT/PATCH requests, produce 404/retry state, or attach the draft to the wrong target.  
+   **Fix:** add a separate phase such as `{ kind: "public-choice", publicCopy }`; do not put its slug in `articleAnswer`, `Completion`, `highPowerSlug`, `shareSlug`, or `purposeFor`. Keep the existing slugless purpose draft alive, then bind High-powered, sharing, and purpose only after the `ownCopy` POST returns the reader’s job/article slug. Test that the choice produces no article mutation requests, that purpose and High-powered intent survive into the own import, that StrictMode sends exactly one initial POST and one chosen POST, and that uploads remain unchanged.
+
+4. **P2 — The plan does not decide what happens when the new lookup fails.**  
+   Evidence: Citations treats `citedCandidates` as an optional enrichment and catches/logs its failure ([routes.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/routes.ts:11425)). The proposed admission path does not state whether the same error becomes a 500 or is treated as a miss. Treating it as a miss may charge a slot even though a public copy exists; letting it escape can make every URL import unavailable because an optional lookup broke.  
+   **Fix:** choose this explicitly. The safer billing behavior is a 503 with no reservation or job, preserving the promise that a lookup failure cannot turn into an unexpected charge. Add a store-failure test asserting the ledger and job table remain unchanged.
+
+5. **P3 — Selection among duplicate public copies is unspecified.**  
+   Evidence: multiple readers can publish copies of the same source, while `citedCandidatesQuery` has no ordering ([pg-cited-in-spideryarn.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/store/pg-cited-in-spideryarn.ts:69)); the plan merely says to keep matching candidates ([plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/plans/261009j-a-public-copy-offered-at-import.md:49)). Taking the first row would make the offered slug/title planner-dependent. Citations already uses slug as its final deterministic tie-break ([cited-in-spideryarn.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/cited-in-spideryarn.ts:181)).  
+   **Fix:** specify and test a deterministic choice—slug order is the simplest consistent rule—and define the title fallback as `displayTitle ?? matchTitle ?? slug`.
+
+6. **P3 — The parser, regression tests, and reference-doc updates are underspecified.**  
+   Evidence: `parseJobRequest` currently destructures only known fields and builds a shared `rest` ([routes.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/routes.ts:6897)); the enqueue path removes only `useProfile` ([routes.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/routes.ts:12641)). The test plan checks only `ownCopy` beside `slug` ([plan](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/plans/261009j-a-public-copy-offered-at-import.md:143)). Several current docs would become false: billing says ordinary `{url}` reserves ([billing.md](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/project/billing.md:938)); the route table says `{url}` always returns a 202 job ([ingest-queue.md](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/project/ingest-queue.md:2347)); Links says one hover-card press spends a slot ([links.md](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/project/links.md:516)); and the MCP table describes only repeats as free ([mcp.md](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/docs/project/mcp.md:67)).  
+   **Fix:** validate `ownCopy` as an actual boolean, reject it with `slug`, `uploadId`, `steps`, `force`, and `readThis`, and strip it before constructing `work`. Test false and wrong-type values, every forbidden combination, `ownCopy: true` when the reader already owns the article, concurrent/retried own-copy requests, and stale Add-page responses after changing address. Update billing, ingest-queue, links, MCP, public-readable-sharing, and security-map. The production callers are otherwise fully identified: AddPage, ProseHoverCard through `useJobs.add`, and MCP `import_article`.
+
+Billing conclusion: `ownCopy` is safe provided it skips only the public offer and still reaches `withIngestSlot`; duplicate live requests do not double-charge because reservations that acquire no job are released ([admission.ts](/var/tmp/spideryarn-worktrees/fbahvk74-import-public-offer/src/billing/admission.ts:265)). The reader’s own-copy lookup must remain first, including when `ownCopy: true`.
+
+ready with changes
